WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.245
Module three. Campaigns. Sending a template to many customers at once, reading the

2
00:00:06.245 --> 00:00:10.229
Results, and sending messages automatically through the API.

3
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:16.947
A campaign is how you send an approved template to a list of customers.

4
00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:21.715
For customer care, you'll use campaigns for updates, reminders and win-back

5
00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:26.992
Messages, and the API for messages that go out automatically when something happens

6
00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:28.390
In the Oribrix system.

7
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.718
First, the three campaign types.

8
00:00:31.168 --> 00:00:33.792
Then a CSV broadcast, step by step.

9
00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:36.802
Then variables, fallback values and media.

10
00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:39.214
Then the cost estimate and the wallet.

11
00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:41.542
Then reading the campaign analytics.

12
00:00:41.992 --> 00:00:45.533
And finally, API campaigns for automatic messages.

13
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:52.349
From Campaigns, click Launch on the top right. You'll see three campaign types.

14
00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:58.090
Broadcast. Send to contacts already saved on the platform, filtered by tags or

15
00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:58.836
Attributes.

16
00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:05.191
CSV broadcast. Upload an Excel or C S V file. Use it when you have a new list of

17
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:05.708
People.

18
00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:11.469
API campaign. The Oribrix system sends the message automatically, one at a time,

19
00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:15.054
When an event happens, like an order being dispatched.

20
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.240
Here's a CSV broadcast from start to finish.

21
00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.250
Click Launch, and choose CSV broadcast.

22
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.306
Give the campaign a clear name, like November dispatch reminder.

23
00:01:27.756 --> 00:01:32.991
Upload the C S V. Two columns are mandatory: the name and the phone number.

24
00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:36.481
Other columns, like product or city, are optional.

25
00:01:36.931 --> 00:01:41.537
Map the columns, so the platform knows which column is the name and which is the

26
00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:42.286
Phone number.

27
00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:46.277
Pick an approved template, and fill its variables from the columns.

28
00:01:46.727 --> 00:01:49.458
Check the estimated cost, then click Send now.

29
00:01:51.867 --> 00:01:56.390
A few details make the difference between a good campaign and an embarrassing one.

30
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.674
Map each variable to a column. For example, variable one to the name column,

31
00:02:01.674 --> 00:02:03.901
Variable two to the product column.

32
00:02:04.351 --> 00:02:08.065
Set a sensible fallback value, used when a cell is empty.

33
00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:12.692
A fallback like customer reads much better than an empty gap or a zero.

34
00:02:13.142 --> 00:02:17.793
If the template has an image or video header, upload the real file at this step.

35
00:02:18.243 --> 00:02:21.681
And keep phone numbers in one format, with the country code.

36
00:02:21.681 --> 00:02:23.171
Wrong numbers simply fail.

37
00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:30.527
Before clicking Send now, the last screen shows the estimated cost, your available

38
00:02:30.527 --> 00:02:34.035
Wallet balance and the price per message. Always check it.

39
00:02:34.035 --> 00:02:37.059
If the wallet is short, the campaign won't finish.

40
00:02:37.059 --> 00:02:42.079
You are charged only for messages that are sent and delivered, not for failed ones.

41
00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:28.095
Click a campaign's name to open its analytics. You'll see when it was launched, how

42
00:03:28.095 --> 00:03:30.223
Long it should take, and these numbers.

43
00:03:30.673 --> 00:03:32.849
Sent. The message left the platform.

44
00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:35.560
Delivered. It reached the customer's phone.

45
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.866
Read. The customer opened it.

46
00:03:38.316 --> 00:03:42.362
Replied or clicked. The customer tapped a button or wrote back.

47
00:03:42.362 --> 00:03:44.546
These replies arrive in live chat.

48
00:03:44.996 --> 00:03:49.068
And failed. The message was not delivered, for example a wrong number.

49
00:03:49.068 --> 00:03:50.756
You're not charged for these.

50
00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:57.135
The campaign page is more than a report. Here's what you can do from it.

51
00:03:57.585 --> 00:04:01.126
See exactly which customers received, read or replied.

52
00:04:01.576 --> 00:04:02.878
Download the report.

53
00:04:03.328 --> 00:04:07.515
Select a group, for example everyone who didn't read it, and re-broadcast a

54
00:04:07.515 --> 00:04:09.301
Different template to just them.

55
00:04:09.751 --> 00:04:11.564
Track which buttons people clicked.

56
00:04:12.014 --> 00:04:15.876
And keep the list of failed numbers, so you can correct them in your records.

57
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:23.911
Now automatic messages through the API. This is how the Oribrix system can send, for

58
00:04:23.911 --> 00:04:28.614
Example, an order dispatched message without anyone pressing a button.

59
00:04:29.064 --> 00:04:31.282
Click Launch, and choose API campaign.

60
00:04:31.732 --> 00:04:36.071
Name the campaign exactly the same as the template, so you can tell them apart

61
00:04:36.071 --> 00:04:36.404
Later.

62
00:04:36.854 --> 00:04:41.845
Click Set live. Every new template you want to send through the API must be set live

63
00:04:41.845 --> 00:04:42.380
This way.

64
00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.878
Go back to Campaigns, and open it.

65
00:04:45.328 --> 00:04:52.084
Copy the c U R L test command. The API key and full documentation are under Manage,

66
00:04:52.084 --> 00:04:53.712
API key, read A P I.

67
00:04:54.162 --> 00:04:57.720
The developers then call it from the Oribrix backend.

68
00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.354
Keep the API key secret: anyone with it can send messages as Oribrix.

69
00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:09.002
Quick check. Your C S V has one thousand rows, and forty numbers fail.

70
00:05:09.002 --> 00:05:12.511
How many messages are you charged for? Think for a moment.

71
00:05:16.461 --> 00:05:21.627
The answer: nine hundred and sixty. You pay only for sent and delivered messages,

72
00:05:21.627 --> 00:05:22.648
Not failed ones.

73
00:05:25.433 --> 00:05:27.182
Let's summarise module three.

74
00:05:27.632 --> 00:05:32.240
Campaigns can be broadcasts, CSV broadcasts, or API campaigns.

75
00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.104
A C S V needs name and phone columns, and you map them.

76
00:05:36.554 --> 00:05:39.732
Fill the variables, set fallbacks, and upload the media.

77
00:05:40.182 --> 00:05:43.980
Check the cost against the wallet. Failed messages aren't charged.

78
00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:49.781
And for the API, name the campaign like the template, set it live, and keep the key

79
00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:53.134
Secret. In module four, live chat and customer care.

80
00:05:55.533 --> 00:06:01.421
That's the end of module 3. Next up, module 4: Live chat, chatbot and customer care.
